As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and April to May came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 202% of normal in April to May, then just 47% in November to December. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 20574 at 58%. For 2026 so far, January to February sat at 44% of normal on the middle of the grids, and June to July reached 158%.</p>"}
